WEBVTT

00:01.280 --> 00:07.220
<i>Danger and opportunity are everywhere in
this place they call the Labyrinth City.</i>

00:07.790 --> 00:14.990
<i>The city itself is a labyrinth, and young
men and women risk their lives there.</i>

00:17.090 --> 00:18.240
<i>My name's Nick.</i>

00:18.240 --> 00:21.990
<i>I'm a Swashbuckler with Masters of War,
a group of skilled adventurers.</i>

00:22.310 --> 00:28.160
<i>I've got a girlfriend, and life is great.
My dream is to make Masters of War an A-Rank party...</i>

00:28.400 --> 00:31.880
Nick, we no longer need you in our party.

00:31.880 --> 00:32.780
What?

00:32.780 --> 00:36.370
<i>Argas, the man I looked up to like a father,
kicked me out of the party.</i>

00:38.530 --> 00:40.620
Let's break up, then!

00:41.490 --> 00:44.920
<i>The girl I thought was my girlfriend
dumped and betrayed me.</i>

00:45.260 --> 00:46.850
<i>And the next thing I knew...</i>

00:47.670 --> 00:49.630
<i>I was an idol otaku!</i>

00:53.970 --> 00:57.670
Agate!

00:59.030 --> 01:10.880
<b><i>Ningen Fushin: Adventurers Who Don't
Believe in Humanity Will Save the World</i></b>

02:33.950 --> 02:36.270
You're the best, Agate!

02:36.270 --> 02:38.630
Now, you all know what our next song is...

02:38.630 --> 02:41.720
The "Saint's Fight Song"!

02:52.850 --> 02:56.260
Why, Argas?

02:56.940 --> 03:00.650
You want me to forgive Garosso, too,
after he stole money from us for some girl?

03:00.650 --> 03:03.180
It's not just Garosso.

03:03.180 --> 03:07.040
You don't think like an adventurer!

03:07.040 --> 03:10.960
You were just a kid when I
took you in and raised you up,

03:10.960 --> 03:13.760
and now you're telling everyone what to do.

03:13.760 --> 03:15.150
What are youâ€”

03:15.150 --> 03:19.430
We're done talking. You and I just
have different ways of doing things.

03:19.430 --> 03:24.630
You aren't a kid anymore.
Go find some place you're better suited to.

03:24.630 --> 03:26.640
Argas, I...

03:32.690 --> 03:37.990
I looked up to you...

03:39.220 --> 03:40.750
You're soaked.

03:51.950 --> 03:53.360
Um...

03:57.660 --> 03:59.670
Don't shoo me off like some stray dog!

04:00.550 --> 04:01.600
Um...

04:06.470 --> 04:09.380
I-I'm an idol!

04:09.930 --> 04:11.790
I don't see it.

04:11.790 --> 04:15.220
I-I'm just getting started,
but I'm working really hard.

04:15.220 --> 04:17.520
No, I don't see why you're talking to me.

04:18.720 --> 04:22.540
An idol's job is to cheer people up
and give them courage!

04:22.540 --> 04:25.360
I'll be at Southgate Hall tomorrow!

04:25.360 --> 04:26.500
I'm not going.

04:27.120 --> 04:30.400
Make sure you're there, Mr. Stray Dog!

04:33.340 --> 04:35.640
I said I wasn't going...

04:37.250 --> 04:39.920
Elly Productions
Fan Appreciation Event
Starring
Garnet Amber Agate Topaz
7:00 PM at Southgate Hall

04:38.520 --> 04:40.840
Agate?

04:40.840 --> 04:43.110
Thank you, everyone!

04:43.110 --> 04:44.500
I'm so glad I came!

04:45.750 --> 04:47.500
Thank you for your purchase!

04:51.510 --> 04:55.190
Agate was just wonderful...

04:59.650 --> 05:05.280
<b>Adventurer's Guild Newbies</b>

05:01.240 --> 05:05.290
Now, time to meet some new friends at
the place where adventurers gather.

05:05.290 --> 05:09.150
If I'm gonna be an idol otaku, I want
to make the money I spend honestly!

05:09.150 --> 05:11.340
Just wait for me, Agate!

05:09.410 --> 05:12.410
<b>Adventurer's Guild Newbies</b>

05:20.540 --> 05:21.420
<b>We at Moon Enjoy are the
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hLEGIT deal!</b>

05:20.540 --> 05:21.420
We may look like
n00bs but we ain't!
yolo iykwim!Â

05:20.540 --> 05:21.420
Moon Mascot

05:20.540 --> 05:21.420
2 Slots available!

05:20.540 --> 05:21.420
Lfg people who
want to be S-Rank!
Only apply if srs!!

05:21.420 --> 05:22.550
<b>US</b>

05:21.420 --> 05:22.550
<b>We've only been
around 4 2 months
but we've got
S-Rank Energy!</b>

05:21.420 --> 05:22.550
<b>Scary-lookin' dudes welcome</b>

05:25.600 --> 05:26.610
<i>Okay!</i>

05:29.560 --> 05:30.670
Yah...

05:30.670 --> 05:32.310
Hm?

05:33.140 --> 05:36.750
<i>Nick, you're not cut out
to be an adventurer.</i>

05:38.050 --> 05:40.180
Yah! Twah!

05:40.180 --> 05:42.430
<i>If only I could namedrop Masters of War...</i>

05:42.430 --> 05:44.950
You want to join a party with me?

05:45.640 --> 05:46.880
Sure!

05:46.880 --> 05:50.200
<i>I can't believe in anyone anymore.</i>

05:50.570 --> 05:52.330
<b>Adventurer's Guild Newbies</b>

05:50.680 --> 05:53.020
Better luck next time!

05:53.830 --> 05:56.310
I couldn't talk to a single person...

06:01.570 --> 06:03.840
Cheers!

06:04.090 --> 06:05.540
It's delicious!

06:05.540 --> 06:09.190
I'll never forget the taste of
the food I shared with you all!

06:09.190 --> 06:11.090
To our new party!

06:11.090 --> 06:12.840
Cheers!

06:14.770 --> 06:15.610
Yuck.

06:17.890 --> 06:21.880
<i>Maybe I can't laugh like that anymore...</i>

06:20.580 --> 06:23.070
Party of three!

06:23.070 --> 06:24.160
Welcome!

06:24.160 --> 06:25.780
Sorry, you'll have to share a table.

06:25.780 --> 06:26.750
Try to get along.

06:26.750 --> 06:30.240
Oh, one stewed mole-pig offal,
coming right up!

06:41.320 --> 06:42.390
<i>A party?</i>

06:44.860 --> 06:46.630
<i>Doesn't look like it...</i>

06:47.700 --> 06:49.140
Hey there!

06:49.140 --> 06:52.000
You want to go on an adventure with me?

06:53.590 --> 06:55.510
I'm so sorry!

06:56.750 --> 07:02.270
<i>That jewel's pretty old. And expensive.</i>

07:02.780 --> 07:07.260
<i>Every item of clothing she's wearing
tells me she's from a rich family,</i>

07:07.640 --> 07:10.640
<i>one that must've loved her a whole lot.</i>

07:10.640 --> 07:14.770
<i>But she sticks out here, badly.</i>

07:15.190 --> 07:17.640
<i>She looks like a mage, but...</i>

07:17.640 --> 07:20.030
<i>Is she an assassin?</i>

07:24.250 --> 07:26.420
<i>And that cleric's been drinking
since before he got here.</i>

07:26.810 --> 07:30.210
<i>With the girls on each side? No.</i>

07:30.210 --> 07:34.810
<i>He just left a cabaret club.
I can still smell their perfume.</i>

07:35.090 --> 07:38.820
<i>And no medal, either,
which means he was excommunicated.</i>

07:39.830 --> 07:43.450
<i>Cleric is a popular job,
and everybody's ignoring him.</i>

07:45.070 --> 07:46.570
<i>And there's a dragonian.</i>

07:47.170 --> 07:49.190
<i>She looks like she's seen
more than her share of battles,</i>

07:49.840 --> 07:51.970
<i>but she reminds me of a wounded animal.</i>

08:06.570 --> 08:10.580
<i>To Argas. To my beautiful girlfriend.</i>

08:11.040 --> 08:13.470
<i>And to the gloomy bastards in front of me.</i>

08:14.630 --> 08:18.460
<i>Screw adventuring. Screw having a girlfriend.</i>

08:18.850 --> 08:21.160
<i>Any friend I make is just
going to betray me later.</i>

08:21.160 --> 08:24.180
<i>I'll never be able to trust anyone.</i>

08:25.050 --> 08:26.680
<i>Argas might be right.</i>

08:27.210 --> 08:30.030
<i>Maybe I'm not cut out to be an adventurer.</i>

08:30.830 --> 08:32.080
<i>But...</i>

08:39.320 --> 08:42.150
You just can't trust anyone!

08:53.990 --> 08:55.360
Lightning Strike!

09:05.250 --> 09:08.250
Just what I'd expect to see from
the daughter of the Erenafelt clan!

09:08.250 --> 09:12.420
You couldn't do that without mastering
both water and wind magic!

09:12.420 --> 09:18.230
I'm not learning magic to become famous
and powerful, but to train my mind.

09:18.230 --> 09:20.440
You're amazing, Tiana.

09:20.690 --> 09:24.960
You've mastered multi-element magic
and still retain your humility.

09:24.960 --> 09:27.830
You're the pride and joy of our school.

09:28.250 --> 09:30.450
Thank you, Master.

09:33.880 --> 09:38.340
<i>Magic doesn't exist just to
make our daily lives easier.</i>

09:38.730 --> 09:42.960
<i>Learning magic means learning
about human society...</i>

09:42.960 --> 09:46.970
<i>and even about our world itself.</i>

09:58.320 --> 09:59.350
Welcome!

09:59.870 --> 10:01.480
Is Alex here?

10:01.480 --> 10:03.230
Um...

10:03.230 --> 10:05.750
It's fine. I'll take some tea.

10:07.460 --> 10:09.750
Oh, Alex, you're so silly!

10:10.520 --> 10:11.650
Alex!

10:13.010 --> 10:14.380
Hello, Tiana.

10:14.380 --> 10:15.980
You're looking cheerful this morning!

10:15.980 --> 10:17.890
I'm feeling cheerful! Get this, Alex!

10:18.400 --> 10:22.020
Did you astonish your teachers
with another amazing spell?

10:22.590 --> 10:25.880
The teachers loved my lightning magic!

10:26.090 --> 10:28.350
I'll be able to graduate a year early!

10:28.350 --> 10:31.400
That's, well...

10:32.070 --> 10:34.750
She's just like the rumors said.

10:36.320 --> 10:37.580
Who's that?

10:37.580 --> 10:41.270
I'm Lynn, the eldest daughter
of the Delcott family.

10:41.270 --> 10:43.660
Oh, those merchants who got rich...

10:43.660 --> 10:46.280
Don't talk to her like that.

10:46.280 --> 10:49.680
I heard you're bullying her at school, too.

10:49.680 --> 10:50.790
Huh?!

10:50.790 --> 10:55.010
Tiana, I know you've got it out for Lynn.

10:55.010 --> 10:56.370
What are you talking about?

10:56.370 --> 10:58.310
You even seduced the school's teachers...

10:58.760 --> 11:03.740
You just insulted not only me,
but the entire school.

11:03.740 --> 11:09.040
The teachers are suspected of taking
bribes to change students' grades.

11:09.040 --> 11:11.220
Th-That's ridiculous...

11:10.400 --> 11:12.480
You need to stop, Tiana!

11:13.270 --> 11:15.180
A-Alex?

11:15.180 --> 11:16.570
It's always the same thing with you.

11:16.970 --> 11:18.920
You're either bragging about your magic

11:18.920 --> 11:21.410
or looking down on people who aren't
as rich and powerful as you.

11:21.410 --> 11:24.520
You always said you were
"working hard for me," right?

11:24.520 --> 11:26.440
Working hard for me? Hah!

11:26.690 --> 11:30.860
Do you know what they're all saying about me
now that you're the school's top student?

11:30.860 --> 11:33.330
I was supposed to be in the
Mages Union like my father,

11:33.330 --> 11:35.970
and now my fiancÃ©e is better than me!

11:35.970 --> 11:37.450
Do you know what they say?

11:38.050 --> 11:39.430
Alex...

11:40.080 --> 11:41.990
It's over.

11:41.990 --> 11:45.320
My engagement to you...
All those days of humiliation...

11:46.160 --> 11:47.090
Tiana...

11:48.370 --> 11:51.480
who was it you were looking at?

12:26.920 --> 12:29.910
<i>Who was it you were looking at?</i>

12:30.310 --> 12:33.690
<i>Who were you seeing in front of you?</i>

12:39.760 --> 12:44.190
<i>Maybe I was only seeing myself.</i>

13:04.520 --> 13:07.420
Sorry, we can't hire anybody
without a letter of recommendation.

13:07.700 --> 13:10.930
A noblewoman wouldn't last a day here.

13:10.930 --> 13:14.520
Sorry, we're not hiring.

13:17.160 --> 13:19.350
It's harder to find a job than I thought.

13:23.030 --> 13:26.280
<b>Your chance to get rich!</b>

13:25.070 --> 13:27.160
<b>Terane Dragon Racetrack Betting Slip</b>

13:27.420 --> 13:30.940
Go! You can do it!

13:27.700 --> 13:30.940
<i>Come on! Come on! Come on!</i>

13:30.940 --> 13:33.410
<i>Come on! Come on!</i>

13:40.020 --> 13:41.290
I won...

13:41.690 --> 13:43.990
<i>That's the scary thing about gambling.</i>

13:44.510 --> 13:48.710
<i>It wasn't long before I went through the
same thing that happens to every gambler.</i>

13:51.390 --> 13:52.560
I lost.

13:56.830 --> 14:00.170
<i>How am I going to pay the rent?</i>

14:04.070 --> 14:06.320
<b>Come be an
adventurer!</b>

14:05.470 --> 14:07.690
Hey, you're a mage, right?

14:09.440 --> 14:11.640
No, never mind! Sorry!

14:15.060 --> 14:17.440
Oops. Gotta remember to smile.

14:17.440 --> 14:18.550
Um...

14:20.080 --> 14:23.060
A monster! Run away!

14:24.060 --> 14:26.570
Party of three!

14:26.570 --> 14:27.830
Welcome!

14:27.350 --> 14:29.270
Sorry, you'll have to share a table.

14:29.270 --> 14:30.230
Try to get along.

14:30.230 --> 14:33.720
Oh, one stewed mole-pig offal,
coming right up!

14:36.410 --> 14:38.110
Your fiancÃ© dumped you, huh?

14:38.110 --> 14:39.600
That's rough.

14:40.020 --> 14:41.480
You're in no position to talk.

14:41.750 --> 14:46.100
Wow, harsh. What about you, Mr. Cleric?

14:51.720 --> 14:52.860
I...

14:54.680 --> 14:56.530
My city is known for its medicinal herbs,

14:56.530 --> 14:59.870
and for its temple worshiping the
god of Divine Inspiration, Medler.

15:00.230 --> 15:02.510
I was a cleric there.

15:03.050 --> 15:04.930
Father Zem! Father Zem!

15:05.620 --> 15:06.750
Look at this!

15:09.400 --> 15:11.510
I even found some Pilchard Grass.

15:11.510 --> 15:13.730
Wonderful.

15:13.730 --> 15:15.220
Thank you, Miril.

15:16.230 --> 15:18.000
Here's a little something for you.

15:22.400 --> 15:24.520
Bye, Father Zem!

15:33.500 --> 15:35.410
Father Zem!

15:35.410 --> 15:36.820
Hello, Miril.

15:36.820 --> 15:38.500
You're later than usual today.

15:38.500 --> 15:40.650
I was working extra hard for you!

15:45.420 --> 15:48.290
Father Zem, do you like me?

15:48.590 --> 15:50.540
You're being a spoiled
little girl today, I see.

15:50.540 --> 15:53.300
No, I'm all grown up!

15:54.230 --> 15:55.630
But...

15:55.630 --> 15:59.170
I want to be more of a grown-up.

16:00.390 --> 16:01.830
Thank you, Miril.

16:02.530 --> 16:07.310
But listen to me. I'm a man of the cloth.

16:07.310 --> 16:10.430
I'm not allowed to date anyone.

16:10.730 --> 16:13.700
You should expend your
efforts for your own sake.

16:17.970 --> 16:19.560
Father Zem, you jerk!

16:19.560 --> 16:21.280
I hate you!

16:32.010 --> 16:35.630
This is your fault, Father Zem.

16:38.530 --> 16:40.950
Thank you, Father Zem.

16:40.950 --> 16:42.230
Not at all...

16:42.680 --> 16:46.250
Oh, I haven't congratulated you yet.

16:46.970 --> 16:50.470
I've heard you're being
promoted to High Cleric!

16:50.960 --> 16:55.630
That's a strange rumor to spread
about a young kid like me.

16:55.630 --> 16:56.660
Out of the way!

16:56.660 --> 16:58.110
Is Zem here?!

16:59.250 --> 17:00.910
What's going on?

17:01.990 --> 17:04.620
Miril! What's wrong?

17:04.620 --> 17:06.240
Poor thing...

17:06.240 --> 17:08.180
Who did this?

17:08.180 --> 17:10.080
Don't play dumb!

17:10.080 --> 17:12.570
You were even paying her!

17:14.180 --> 17:15.880
M-Miril!

17:16.570 --> 17:20.020
I believed in you, Father Zem!

17:23.710 --> 17:24.510
Miril...

17:31.290 --> 17:34.570
Are you too good for the
food here, <i>Your Holiness</i>?

17:35.110 --> 17:36.540
Three months.

17:37.230 --> 17:40.080
I was in there for three months
before being banished.

17:40.440 --> 17:43.750
Nobody believed I was innocent.

17:43.750 --> 17:46.160
Get out of our city, pervert!

17:48.660 --> 17:51.290
I was a fool to believe in you!

18:01.790 --> 18:04.930
Oh, Father! Welcome!

18:04.930 --> 18:07.170
Are you on a pilgrimage?

18:08.660 --> 18:10.270
Something like that.

18:14.030 --> 18:16.320
Are you in need of healing?

18:38.590 --> 18:40.210
Did you sleep well?

18:41.500 --> 18:44.220
Thanks to you, the pain in my back is gone.

18:44.780 --> 18:46.320
You saw for yourself, right?

18:56.170 --> 18:57.970
You shouldn't overwork yourself.

18:57.970 --> 19:01.870
Chronic back pain takes time to heal.

19:03.180 --> 19:06.240
You'll have to stay here
a little longer, then.

19:07.020 --> 19:08.140
That was a joke.

19:08.550 --> 19:12.880
You should go to Labyrinth City
and become an adventurer.

19:14.380 --> 19:17.820
Make friends. Fall in love.

19:17.820 --> 19:20.380
Let loose once in a while.

19:20.960 --> 19:23.630
Go out and see the world.

19:23.630 --> 19:25.470
You're not a criminal.

19:28.000 --> 19:29.090
Right?

19:29.670 --> 19:32.370
But I...

19:33.550 --> 19:36.760
Oh, I've got something for you.

19:41.180 --> 19:43.200
I can't accept this.

19:44.430 --> 19:47.400
Think of it as a donation
to the church, Father.

19:48.610 --> 19:51.050
"Former" Father.

19:51.540 --> 19:54.800
Some idiot stayed here once and left
it as collateral for the room charge.

19:57.600 --> 19:58.950
You have to live, don't you?

20:00.210 --> 20:01.050
Right.

20:01.910 --> 20:05.940
And then you took a bit too much of
a liking to the ladies, is that it?

20:05.940 --> 20:10.630
That's a rude way to put it,
but yes, essentially.

20:11.500 --> 20:14.060
Maybe all guys are like that.

20:17.610 --> 20:21.800
Well, I can't believe
everything you guys say.

20:21.800 --> 20:24.160
They're just stories told over a mug of beer.

20:24.160 --> 20:28.070
Stories from people I'll never
see again after tonight.

20:28.690 --> 20:30.530
It's the same for you all, right?

20:30.530 --> 20:33.090
Yes, that's true.

20:33.550 --> 20:37.290
I'm actually going to defeat
the Demon King after this.

20:39.920 --> 20:40.830
And?

20:41.300 --> 20:42.680
Is it your turn?

20:45.830 --> 20:47.290
I...

20:51.870 --> 20:56.780
Something important was stolen from me...

20:56.780 --> 20:59.010
By the person who was
most important to me...

20:59.760 --> 21:05.400
So I says to the guy, I says,
"You can't take it!"

21:03.700 --> 21:05.440
She's falling-down drunk...

21:05.400 --> 21:06.570
Are you listening?

21:06.560 --> 21:08.820
Yes, I'm listening!

21:08.820 --> 21:12.470
So anyway, I says to him...

21:13.700 --> 21:15.840
Wow...

21:16.120 --> 21:18.720
You're the best!

21:19.010 --> 21:20.280
So,

21:21.540 --> 21:22.850
let's break up, then!

21:22.850 --> 21:24.870
What are you talking about?

21:26.210 --> 21:28.470
Girls don't like pushy guys!

21:29.190 --> 21:30.480
Why do you have that?!

21:32.380 --> 21:36.700
Nick, you really were... the best
mark for a con I've ever met!

21:36.700 --> 21:38.200
Wait, Claudine!

21:38.200 --> 21:40.880
Tell me it's not true!

21:43.500 --> 21:45.740
Ow...

21:51.010 --> 21:53.360
<i>Who are these people?</i>

21:54.210 --> 21:56.300
I can't eat another bite...

21:59.750 --> 22:02.010
You just can't trust anyone!

22:05.130 --> 22:07.540
So, who the hell are you?

22:07.540 --> 22:08.520
Get out of here.

22:08.520 --> 22:10.370
Also, where the hell am I?

22:10.370 --> 22:14.380
I'm Tiana the mage, and this is my room.

22:14.380 --> 22:16.280
You need to leave, not me.

22:17.840 --> 22:19.200
'Kay, bye.

22:19.200 --> 22:20.780
I've embarrassed myself so badly...

22:20.780 --> 22:21.760
Sorry.

22:30.910 --> 22:33.710
I-I'm an idol!

22:36.360 --> 22:37.780
Wait...

22:40.080 --> 22:41.490
Wait a second!

22:41.490 --> 22:43.040
Is this really okay?

22:43.340 --> 22:44.540
What?

22:45.270 --> 22:49.010
If we split up, can we make
enough money to survive?

22:53.440 --> 22:55.990
Whether it's being an idol otaku,
or eating too much fancy food,

22:55.990 --> 22:58.060
or gambling, or carousing with girls...

22:58.060 --> 23:02.490
We don't even know if we'll have enough
money to rent a room the next day,

23:02.490 --> 23:04.320
let alone do the things we love!

23:04.520 --> 23:08.000
Is it okay for us to just live like that?

23:08.000 --> 23:09.190
Are you okay with that?

23:09.190 --> 23:13.230
Do the things we love mean so little to us?

23:14.710 --> 23:15.830
But that doesn't mean...

23:16.530 --> 23:17.790
So why don't we...

23:18.320 --> 23:20.880
